abel\">\n                        Used By\n                    </div>\n\n                    <h3>\n        <a href=\"/pokemon/pokeball\" class=\"entity-link\">\n            Poké Ball\n        </a>\n    </h3>\n\n                    <p>Poké Balls define catching gameplay.</p>\n\n                    \n\n                    \n                </div>\n            \n        </div>\n    </details>\n</section>\n\n</section>\n\n\n<section class=\"did-you-know\">\n    <h2>Did you know?</h2>\n    <ul>\n        <li>Pokémon is also referenced as Pokemon, Pocket Monsters.</li><li>Pikachu is the franchise mascot.</li><li>Satoshi Tajiri created Pokémon.</li><li>Red and Blue launched the series.</li><li>Pokémon Anime is a medium branch of Pokémon.</li><li>Evidence around Pokémon is classified as fiction on Ton-o-Lore.</li>\n    </ul>\n</section>\n\n\n<section class=\"sources\">\n    <h2>Sources &amp; further reading</h2>\n    <p><a href=\"https://pokemon.fandom.com/wiki/Pok%C3%A9mon\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Fandom wiki</a></p>\n</section>","overview":"<section class=\"overview\">\n    <h2>What is Pokémon?</h2>\n    <p>\n        <strong>Pokémon</strong> is the creature-collecting franchise from\n        <a href=\"/pokemon/game-freak\" class=\"entity-link\">Game Freak</a> and\n        <a href=\"/pokemon/nintendo\" class=\"entity-link\">Nintendo</a>,\n        where trainers like\n        <a href=\"/pokemon/pallet-town/ash-ketchum\" class=\"entity-link\">Ash Ketchum</a>\n        partner with\n        <a href=\"/pokemon/pallet-town/ash-ketchum/pikachu\" class=\"entity-link\">Pikachu</a>\n        across regions such as\n        <a href=\"/pokemon/kanto\" class=\"entity-link\">Kanto</a>.\n    </p>\n</section>","word_count":973,"uniqueness_score":"1.0000"},"entity":{"id":"8bfd767b-a763-4d58-9b52-8a68e3765b69","name":"Pokémon","slug":"pokemon","type":"work","kind":"series","type_label":"Series","short_description":"Pokémon is a Japanese media franchise consisting of video games, animated series and films, a trading card game, and other related media. The franchise takes place in a shared universe in which humans co-exist with the…","description":"It centers around a group of fantasy creatures known as Pokémon, from which the series itself takes its name. A group of humans known as Pokémon Trainers catch Pokémon and train them to battle other Pokémon for sport and/or as loyal companions, with their main goal is to become the Pokémon Champion while preventing a wicked group of Trainers known as villainous teams from causing danger to the world. Although Pokémon is technically a series, similar to Final Fantasy, Dragon Quest, Phantasy Star and others, an animation series, manga, and a trading card game also make up large aspects of the franchise. Pokémon is managed by The Pokémon Company, a company formed by Nintendo, Game Freak, and Creatures Inc.. It is one of Nintendo's flagship franchises, alongside Mario and The Legend of Zelda. The series as a whole debuted with on February 27, 1996 in Japan and in September 1998 in North America, on the original Game Boy. The main mascot of the Pokémon franchise is the yellow Generation I Electric-type mouse Pokémon named Pikachu.\n\nThe main series in the franchise is the eponymous Pokémon series, consisting of RPG games that typically involve a player character (whose name is decided by the player) starting their journey as a Pokémon Trainer after receiving their First partner Pokémon from the Pokémon Professor at the local Pokémon Lab. The professor also gives them a Pokédex, and tasks them to fill it with data entries on Pokémon to aid their research; this is accomplished by obtaining every Pokémon species within that game. The mainline games overall debuted with Pokémon Red Version and Pokémon Green Version, followed by a Blue Version upgrade (Pokémon Red Version and Pokémon Blue Version in non-Japanese localizations) and every installment since had been released in pairs (sometimes having a special edition version shortly after, such as or ). Although the two paired games are identical, the main difference between them is the type of Pokémon encountered, and therefore, it is impossible to collect every Pokémon and complete the Pokédex in one game without trading Pokémon with other players between individual versions, itself a contributing factor of its popularity. Every main Pokémon series installment has been released for a Nintendo handheld device until for the Nintendo Switch, a hybrid home console with a portable handheld mode.","evidence":"fiction","universe":"pokemon","aliases":["Pokemon","Pokémon","Pocket Monsters"],"wikipedia_url":null,"image_url":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/pokemon/images/e/ee/Pocket_Monsters_Red.jpg/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/360?cb=20250109135504","image_source":"https://pokemon.fandom.com/wiki/Pok%C3%A9mon_(franchise)","image_credit":"Fair-use identification thumbnail via Fandom. Character / franchise art © Nintendo / Creatures / Game Freak (as applicable). Not free or redistributable artwork.","image_license":"fair_use","image_usage":"fair_use_identification","image_alt":"Identification thumbnail for Pokémon (franchise)"},"connections":[],"rabbit_holes":[],"copyright":{"theme":"pokemon","title":"Pokémon is not owned by Ton-o-Lore.","body":"Pokémon and all related names, characters, and imagery are trademarks of Nintendo, Game Freak, Creatures, and/or The Pokémon Company. Ton-o-Lore is an independent, unofficial fan and informational project and is not affiliated with or endorsed by those rights holders. Identification logos and thumbnails, when shown, are low-resolution images used under a fair-use rationale for commentary and identification only — not free or redistributable artwork."},"subject":{"id":"pokemon","name":"Pokémon","theme":"pokemon","path":"/pokemon","logo":{"license":"fair_use","usage":"fair_use_identification","url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/International_Pok%C3%A9mon_logo.svg/330px-International_Pok%C3%A9mon_logo.svg.png","alt":"Pokémon logo","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pok%C3%A9mon","credit":"Fair-use identification logo via Wikipedia / Wikimedia Commons. © Nintendo / Game Freak / Creatures / The Pokémon Company."},"categories":["video-games","anime","movies","card-games"]}}